  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with pca_n2000 (config_001) achieves 0.485 acc, far exceeding both image-only baselines (~0.21-0.23), establishing RNA as the dominant modality. However, we have only tested one RNA encoder (pca_n2000, a linear projection). Uncertainty: whether a learned non-linear encoder (scvi_n200) captures richer single-cell structure that translates to better classification. This experiment (config_004: rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_001, isolating the RNA encoder choice while holding profile setting constant. It is the best use of the next budget slot because (1) it directly tests whether encoder sophistication matters before investing in more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations, (2) a positive result would justify exploring scvi_n200 in multimodal settings, while a null result would confirm pca_n2000 is sufficient and redirect effort toward profile aggregation or fusion strategies, and (3) it reduces uncertainty on a foundational design axis that underlies many downstream configuration choices."
}

